{sov: Notes}
Herbie Hancock’s funk-fusion classic is anchored by a modal two-chord groove
in Bb minor / Bb Dorian.  The main groove alternates between Bbm7 (or Bbm9)
and Eb7 (or Eb13). During the extended keyboard solos, the second chord
frequently shifts to a suspended Db7sus4 (often voiced as Bmaj7/Db) to
give Herbie that iconic open, modal color.

Voicing Tip: To get the true Head Hunters sound on the solo section,
try playing Db7sus4 as a Bmaj7 triad with a Db in the bass (Bmaj7/Db).

Soloing: Improvise using Bb Dorian or Bb Minor Blues across both sections.
{eov}